# SpendFlow Project Rules

## Structure

- `ui/` = Next.js frontend only. No DB, Plaid secrets, or business rules.
- `ios/` = SwiftUI iPhone app. Keychain for tokens; native Plaid Link; same API.
- `backend/` = Fastify API + workers. Owns all persistence and Plaid server calls.
- `docs/design/` = requirements source of truth. Update docs when changing behavior.
- `docs/design/design-tokens.json` = shared colors/categories for web and iOS.
- API shape lives in `docs/design/api-contract.md` — keep all clients aligned.

## TypeScript (all services)

- Enable strict mode. No `any`; use `unknown` + type guards at boundaries.
- Validate external input with Zod (API bodies, env vars, webhooks).
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; use `type` for unions and utilities.
- Use explicit return types on exported functions and public APIs.
- Never swallow errors — log with context and rethrow or map to HTTP errors.

## Scope discipline

- Minimal diffs. No speculative helpers or premature abstractions.
- Match existing naming: kebab-case files, PascalCase React components.
- Do not commit `.env` files or secrets.

## Phase 0

Structure and rules only until scaffolding is explicitly requested. Read `AGENTS.md` before implementing.
